# ============================================================================
# gts4lv / gts4lvwifi defconfig fragment for LineageOS 23.2 (Android 16)
#
# task:     K6 (round 2)
# sources:  sdm670 = a30605a54f3b, series base = d54533f1546b,
#           series head = baa585f67e0e
# target:   arch/arm64/configs/gts4lv_defconfig
#           arch/arm64/configs/gts4lvwifi_defconfig
#           (identical for every line used here - verified with diff)
#
# NOTE: this is a FRAGMENT. Nothing here was applied to any kernel tree.
#       The lead appends it. APPEND, do not prepend: kconfig's conf_read_simple
#       lets a later line override an earlier one for the same symbol, which is
#       how section 4 switches off lines that are already =y at gts4lv_defconfig
#       :28 (RT_GROUP_SCHED) and :34 (SCHED_TUNE).
#
# counts:   33 CONFIG_*=y lines
#             = 14 requested "turn on"
#             +  1 correction from round 1  (UPROBES)
#             +  8 dependencies not present as explicit lines today
#             + 10 dependencies already satisfied, re-stated for self-containment
#           3 "# CONFIG_* is not set" lines (the 3 requested "turn off")
# ============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOCKER 1 of 3 - CONFIG_UNICODE=y below is a NO-OP until someone copies code.
#
# fs/unicode/ exists in the series base d54533f1546b (10 files) and at the head
# baa585f67e0e, but it is ABSENT from sdm670, and
#     git log --oneline d54533f1546b..baa585f67e0e -- fs/unicode/   -> 0 commits
# so the 2,599-commit series never brings it. The Kconfig entry will therefore
# not even exist after the cherry-pick, and fs/Makefile:96 @ baa585f67e0e
# ("obj-$(CONFIG_UNICODE) += unicode/") would be missing too.
# To make it real, copy fs/unicode/ from d54533f1546b and add the fs/Makefile
# line. Until then, drop the CONFIG_UNICODE=y line - f2fs/ext4 NFD (casefold,
# compression) support will be missing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOCKER 2 of 3 - CONFIG_BPF_LSM=y is SILENTLY DROPPED without 4 extra lines.
#
# init/Kconfig:1950-1955 @ baa585f67e0e gives four separate "depends on":
# BPF_EVENTS, BPF_SYSCALL, SECURITY, BPF_JIT. None of the four is present in
# gts4lv_defconfig except BPF_SYSCALL (:42) and SECURITY (:793). BPF_JIT is
# "default n" and BPF_EVENTS is a no-prompt bool that itself needs
# (KPROBE_EVENTS || UPROBE_EVENTS) && PERF_EVENTS. Without them kconfig drops
# BPF_LSM with no error and no warning - the LSM hooks just do not exist.
# That is why sections 2.1-2.4 below exist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOCKER 3 of 3 - CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHED=y is not optional, it is MANDATORY.
#
# init/Kconfig:1269 @ baa585f67e0e "menuconfig CGROUP_SCHED ... default n".
# It is needed for UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP (init/Kconfig:1308).
# It is ALSO needed to keep SCHED_WALT=y (gts4lv_defconfig:6) alive:
#   - sdm670  init/Kconfig:407-410 @ a30605a54f3b: SCHED_WALT depends on SMP only
#   - Exy     init/Kconfig:402-406 @ baa585f67e0e:  SCHED_WALT depends on SMP
#                                                       && FAIR_GROUP_SCHED
# The series does NOT add that dependency (git log -S over the series range
# finds nothing; it already exists at the series base d54533f1546b, and in
# sdm670 it only ever existed as part of upstream CFS, never in the Android
# WALT commit 26c2154816c7). But the series rewrites init/Kconfig right next to
# SCHED_WALT (it adds SCHED_WALT_DEFAULT at init/Kconfig:412 @ baa585f67e0e),
# so the merged tree could end up with either form depending on how that hunk
# resolves. If the Exy form wins and CGROUP_SCHED is n, walt.o silently stops
# being built and the tablet loses its scheduler.
# Setting CGROUP_SCHED=y makes SCHED_WALT survive under BOTH resolutions.
#
# Side effect to watch: FAIR_GROUP_SCHED is "default CGROUP_SCHED"
# (init/Kconfig:1278-1281), so CGROUP_SCHED=y also turns FAIR_GROUP_SCHED=y,
# i.e. FAIR group scheduling is now built next to SCHED_WALT. That combination
# is what the series head is built with on Exynos (except Exy has no WALT, it
# uses SCHED_EMS). sdm670 has the guard "depends on !SCHED_WALT" on CFS_BANDWIDTH
# (init/Kconfig:1191 @ a30605a54f3b) which the Exy tree does NOT have. That guard
# is sdm670-local Android work (d342ee64906f / e032df4b1246, reverted by
# 45be79a2ec16, present again at the tip) and is at risk in the same merge.
# CFS_BANDWIDTH itself stays "default n" and this fragment does NOT turn it on,
# so nothing breaks today - but do NOT "fix" a WALT scheduler build error by
# setting # CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED is not set: that would also switch SCHED_WALT
# off on the Exy form of the Kconfig, and would kill UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP's ability
# to sit on a live CGROUP_SCHED. Leave CFS_BANDWIDTH off; that is the fix.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 1 - the 14 requested "turn on" options, plus the UPROBES correction
# =============================================================================

# ANDROID_BINDERFS - drivers/android/Kconfig:22 @ baa585f67e0e
#   added by series commit c286cded153a; code drivers/android/binderfs.c (705
#   lines), Makefile entry drivers/android/Makefile:3 @ baa585f67e0e.
#   CLASSIC ANDROID TRAP: it sits inside "if ANDROID" (drivers/android/Kconfig:8)
#   and its only dep is ANDROID_BINDER_IPC. Both are re-stated in section 3.
#   Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig - it arrives with the series.
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDERFS=y

# BPF_LSM - init/Kconfig:1950 @ baa585f67e0e
#   added by series commit eb8726624efa (kernel/bpf/bpf_lsm.c, security/bpf/).
#   deps: BPF_EVENTS, BPF_SYSCALL, SECURITY, BPF_JIT (init/Kconfig:1952-1955).
#   See BLOCKER 2. Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig.
CONFIG_BPF_LSM=y

# CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED - block/Kconfig.iosched:35 @ baa585f67e0e (same line in sdm670)
#   deps: IOSCHED_CFQ && BLK_CGROUP (block/Kconfig.iosched:37).
#   Already =y at gts4lv_defconfig:59; re-stated so the fragment is self-contained.
#   NOT in either *_eur_open_defconfig, and they have "# CONFIG_BLK_CGROUP is not
#   set" (:151), so both deps must be pinned - see section 2.6/2.7.
CONFIG_CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED=y

# DEBUG_INFO_BTF - lib/Kconfig.debug:177 @ baa585f67e0e
#   added by series commits 8a953036e3b5 (+ ae25ca2f3a61 for modules).
#   dep: DEBUG_INFO (lib/Kconfig.debug:179).
#   *** HOST TOOL REQUIRED: needs pahole on PATH. scripts/link-vmlinux.sh:209,214
#       @ baa585f67e0e fails the vmlinux link if pahole is missing or older than
#       v1.13. PAHOLE=pahole at Makefile:366 @ baa585f67e0e, so it is NOT the
#       distribution's pahole unless PATH says so.
#   *** Also builds a new host tool: Makefile:1239-1249 @ baa585f67e0e builds
#       tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/ under "ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF". That tool
#       does not exist in sdm670; it arrives with series commit d7b603054c46.
#   Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig.
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y

# FUSE_BPF - fs/fuse/Kconfig:20 @ baa585f67e0e
#   added by series commit 462a37becb45 (fs/fuse/backing.c, xattr_bpf.c);
#   Makefile entry fs/fuse/Makefile:9 @ baa585f67e0e.
#   deps: FUSE_FS, BPF_SYSCALL (fs/fuse/Kconfig:22-23).
#   Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig.
CONFIG_FUSE_BPF=y

# KPROBES - arch/Kconfig:43 @ baa585f67e0e (same line in sdm670)
#   deps: MODULES, HAVE_KPROBES (arch/arm64/Kconfig:101 @ baa585f67e0e selects
#   HAVE_KPROBES). select KALLSYMS (arch/Kconfig:47) - see section 2.5.
#   Unset in gts4lvwifi_defconfig and gts4lv_defconfig today; explicitly
#   "# CONFIG_KPROBES is not set" in gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:233.
#   Android 16's bpfloader loads kprobe-based programs, so this is not optional.
CONFIG_KPROBES=y

# NET_ACT_BPF - net/sched/Kconfig:728 @ baa585f67e0e (same line in sdm670)
#   dep: NET_CLS_ACT (net/sched/Kconfig:730) - re-stated in section 3.8.
#   tristate; "is not set" in gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:1140.
CONFIG_NET_ACT_BPF=y

# PSI - init/Kconfig:494 @ baa585f67e0e = init/Kconfig:486 @ a30605a54f3b
#   no deps. Already =y at gts4lv_defconfig:11. NOT in the eur_open files
#   ("# CONFIG_PSI is not set", :108). Android needs /proc/pressure.
CONFIG_PSI=y

# UCLAMP_TASK - init/Kconfig:972 @ baa585f67e0e
#   added by series commit 74b2f258866b.
#   dep: CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL (init/Kconfig:974) - re-stated in section 3.9;
#   that itself needs CPU_FREQ=y (gts4lv_defconfig:95) and SMP (arm64 def_bool y).
#   Turning this on makes SCHED_TUNE impossible: init/Kconfig:1520-1522 has
#   "depends on !UCLAMP_TASK". See section 4.3.
#   Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig.
CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK=y

# UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP - init/Kconfig:1307 @ baa585f67e0e
#   added by series commit ed50d477d59a.
#   deps: CGROUP_SCHED, UCLAMP_TASK (init/Kconfig:1308-1309). Sits OUTSIDE the
#   "if CGROUP_SCHED" block, so it is visible even when CGROUP_SCHED is n - and
#   silently dropped. See BLOCKER 3 / section 2.8.
#   Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig.
CONFIG_UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP=y

# UNICODE - fs/unicode/Kconfig:4 @ baa585f67e0e. No deps.
#   *** NO-OP. See BLOCKER 1 at the top of this file. ***
#   Does NOT exist in sdm670's Kconfig, and neither does the code behind it.
CONFIG_UNICODE=y

# USERFAULTFD - init/Kconfig:2009 @ baa585f67e0e = init/Kconfig:1860 @ a30605a54f3b
#   dep: MMU (init/Kconfig:2011) - re-stated in section 3.10. Android's
#   in-kernel app allocator (heapti/scion) needs this.
#   "is not set" in gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:208.
CONFIG_USERFAULTFD=y

# XDP_SOCKETS - net/xdp/Kconfig:2 @ baa585f67e0e
#   NEW in this task's option list (round 1 left it out).
#   added by series commit f787c74339cb (net/xdp/, 4367 insertions).
#   Fully plumbed: net/Makefile:16 @ baa585f67e0e is
#   "obj-$(CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS) += xdp/", so unlike UNICODE this one really
#   builds. dep: BPF_SYSCALL (net/xdp/Kconfig:4) - re-stated in section 3.3.
#   Not in sdm670's Kconfig and not in net/xdp/ at all.
CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS=y

# XDP_SOCKETS_DIAG - net/xdp/Kconfig:12 @ baa585f67e0e
#   NEW in this task's option list (round 1 left it out).
#   dep: XDP_SOCKETS (net/xdp/Kconfig:14). tristate; "=y" builds net/xdp/xsk_diag.c
#   (net/xdp/Makefile:4 @ baa585f67e0e). Gives PF_XDP monitoring for ss(8).
#   Not in sdm670's Kconfig.
CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS_DIAG=y

# UPROBES - arch/Kconfig:100 @ baa585f67e0e (same line in sdm670)
#   *** CORRECTION TO ROUND 1. Round 1 said this config was optional. It is not. ***
#   config UPROBES is "def_bool n" in BOTH trees (arch/Kconfig:100 @ baa585f67e0e
#   and @ a30605a54f3b) and has NO "depends on KPROBES" - it is independently
#   off, so CONFIG_KPROBES=y above does not bring it.
#   Without it, series commit 2d6869d3a4ce ("arm64: Add uprobe support") is dead
#   code: arch/arm64/kernel/probes/uprobes.c (216 lines), the Makefile entry
#   "obj-$(CONFIG_UPROBES) += uprobes.o" (arch/arm64/kernel/probes/Makefile @ head)
#   and the arch/arm64/kernel/signal.c hook all compile to nothing.
#   Android 16's bpfloader uses uprobes.
#   Its prerequisite ARCH_SUPPORTS_UPROBES (arch/arm64/Kconfig:248 @ baa585f67e0e,
#   "def_bool y") also does not exist in sdm670 - it arrives with 2d6869d3a4ce.
#   Unset in the small defconfigs; "# CONFIG_UPROBES is not set" in
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:235.
CONFIG_UPROBES=y


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 2 - dependencies that are NOT explicit lines in gts4lv_defconfig today
#             These are the lines that make section 1 actually take effect.
# =============================================================================

# --- 2.1 for BPF_LSM (via BPF_EVENTS) ---------------------------------------
# PERF_EVENTS - init/Kconfig:2063 @ baa585f67e0e. Required by BPF_EVENTS
#   (kernel/trace/Kconfig:482). dep HAVE_PERF_EVENTS (arch/arm64/Kconfig:95
#   selects it).
#   NOTE, correcting round 1: this is NOT really missing. init/Kconfig:2065 says
#   "default y if PROFILING" and gts4lv_defconfig:46 already has
#   CONFIG_PROFILING=y (gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:231 too). So PERF_EVENTS is
#   already y by default and kconfig would satisfy it on its own. Pinned anyway so
#   the BPF_LSM chain does not depend on PROFILING staying enabled.
CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS=y

# --- 2.2 for BPF_LSM (via BPF_EVENTS) ---------------------------------------
# KPROBE_EVENTS - kernel/trace/Kconfig:445 @ baa585f67e0e. The other half of
#   BPF_EVENTS' "(KPROBE_EVENTS || UPROBE_EVENTS)" (kernel/trace/Kconfig:482).
#   deps: KPROBES, HAVE_REGS_AND_STACK_ACCESS_API (arch/arm64/Kconfig:98 selects
#   it). select TRACING and PROBE_EVENTS (kernel/trace/Kconfig:449-450);
#   "default y" (:451) so it follows KPROBES automatically.
#   It lives inside "if TRACING_SUPPORT" (kernel/trace/Kconfig:123-719). That is
#   reachable on arm64: TRACING_SUPPORT (kernel/trace/Kconfig) needs
#   TRACE_IRQFLAGS_SUPPORT || PPC32 and STACKTRACE_SUPPORT, and arm64 defines
#   both as "def_bool y" at arch/arm64/Kconfig:176 and :186 @ baa585f67e0e.
#   SIDE EFFECT: TRACING selects DEBUG_FS, RING_BUFFER, TRACEPOINTS,
#   NOP_TRACER, BINARY_PRINTF, EVENT_TRACING and TRACE_CLOCK. None is in
#   gts4lv_defconfig today; all come in via select and the kernel grows.
#   Unavoidable if BPF_LSM is wanted. UPROBE_EVENTS (kernel/trace/Kconfig:463)
#   is the alternative to this line and would "select UPROBES", but it is not
#   needed and pulls in more.
CONFIG_KPROBE_EVENTS=y

# --- 2.3 for BPF_LSM --------------------------------------------------------
# BPF_EVENTS - kernel/trace/Kconfig:480 @ baa585f67e0e. Direct dep of BPF_LSM
#   (init/Kconfig:1952). deps BPF_SYSCALL and
#   (KPROBE_EVENTS || UPROBE_EVENTS) && PERF_EVENTS (:481-482).
#   no-prompt bool, "default y" (:483-484), so it follows 2.1+2.2. Listed so the
#   chain is readable top to bottom instead of implicit.
CONFIG_BPF_EVENTS=y

# --- 2.4 for BPF_LSM - THE ONE THAT REALLY MATTERS ---------------------------
# BPF_JIT - net/Kconfig:297 @ baa585f67e0e. Direct dep of BPF_LSM
#   (init/Kconfig:1955). "default n" - it is genuinely off today, and
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:1170 even says "# CONFIG_BPF_JIT is not set".
#   deps: HAVE_CBPF_JIT || HAVE_EBPF_JIT (arm64 selects HAVE_EBPF_JIT,
#   arch/arm64/Kconfig:73), MODULES, !CFI (net/Kconfig:299-301). arm64 has no CFI
#   in the series head, so !CFI holds.
#   Without this line BPF_LSM is dropped, full stop.
CONFIG_BPF_JIT=y

# --- 2.5 for KPROBES --------------------------------------------------------
# KALLSYMS - init/Kconfig:1787 @ baa585f67e0e. "select"ed by KPROBES
#   (arch/Kconfig:47). "default y" (:1789) but not pinned in gts4lv_defconfig.
#   Listed because gts4lv_defconfig:41 has CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL=y, which needs
#   both KALLSYMS (init/Kconfig:1797) and DEBUG_KERNEL (lib/Kconfig.debug:424).
#   DEBUG_KERNEL is NOT in gts4lv_defconfig and has no default, so KALLSYMS_ALL is
#   currently a dead line; only gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:5516 sets
#   CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y. That is pre-existing, not caused by this fragment.
CONFIG_KALLSYMS=y

# --- 2.6 for CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED ----------------------------------------------
# IOSCHED_CFQ - block/Kconfig.iosched:24 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of
#   CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED (block/Kconfig.iosched:37). tristate, "default y" (:26),
#   so kconfig satisfies it, but not pinned in gts4lv_defconfig.
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:355 has it explicitly.
CONFIG_IOSCHED_CFQ=y

# --- 2.7 for CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED ----------------------------------------------
# BLK_CGROUP - init/Kconfig:1234 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED
#   (block/Kconfig.iosched:37). "default n" (:1237).
#   ALREADY =y at gts4lv_defconfig:27 / gts4lvwifi_defconfig:27, but both
#   *_eur_open_defconfig have "# CONFIG_BLK_CGROUP is not set" (:151). So this
#   line is what makes CFQ_GROUP_IOSCHED work on the eur_open files.
#   dep: BLOCK - "def_bool y", and both eur_open files pin CONFIG_BLOCK=y (:317).
#   SIDE EFFECT on eur_open only: CGROUP_WRITEBACK (init/Kconfig:1263-1267) is
#   "depends on MEMCG && BLK_CGROUP, default y" and is in neither defconfig, so
#   it switches itself on for the eur_open configs. Harmless (writeback throttling),
#   but it is a code-size change to be aware of.
CONFIG_BLK_CGROUP=y

# --- 2.8 for UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP - see BLOCKER 3 ------------------------------
# CGROUP_SCHED - init/Kconfig:1269 @ baa585f67e0e, "menuconfig CGROUP_SCHED
#   ... default n". (It is a menuconfig, so "git grep ^config CGROUP_SCHED$"
#   finds nothing - grep for "^menuconfig CGROUP_SCHED$".)
#   dep of UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP (init/Kconfig:1308) and of RT_GROUP_SCHED
#   (init/Kconfig:1295). NOT in gts4lv_defconfig today; the two *_eur_open files
#   already have CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHED=y (:152) and CONFIG_FAIR_GROUP_SCHED=y (:153).
#   Also required to keep SCHED_WALT=y alive under the Exy form of the Kconfig -
#   see BLOCKER 3.
CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHED=y


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 3 - dependencies already satisfied. Re-stated so this fragment is
#             self-contained and can be appended to any of the four defconfigs.
#             Line numbers are gts4lv_defconfig @ a30605a54f3b.
# =============================================================================

# --- 3.1 for ANDROID_BINDERFS -----------------------------------------------
# ANDROID - drivers/android/Kconfig:3 @ baa585f67e0e. Opens the "menu Android" /
#   "if ANDROID" (:8) that ANDROID_BINDER_IPC and ANDROID_BINDERFS live inside.
#   Without it both are invisible. Present at gts4lv_defconfig:704,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:5072.
CONFIG_ANDROID=y

# --- 3.2 for ANDROID_BINDERFS -----------------------------------------------
# ANDROID_BINDER_IPC - drivers/android/Kconfig:10 @ baa585f67e0e. The only dep of
#   ANDROID_BINDERFS (:23); itself needs MMU && !M68K (:12). Present at
#   gts4lv_defconfig:705, gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:5073.
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC=y

# --- 3.3 for BPF_LSM, FUSE_BPF, XDP_SOCKETS, BPF_EVENTS ----------------------
# BPF_SYSCALL - init/Kconfig:1938 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of BPF_LSM (init/Kconfig:
#   1953), FUSE_BPF (fs/fuse/Kconfig:23), XDP_SOCKETS (net/xdp/Kconfig:4) and
#   BPF_EVENTS (kernel/trace/Kconfig:481). Present at gts4lv_defconfig:42,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:204.
CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y

# --- 3.4 for BPF_LSM ---------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY - security/Kconfig:30 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of BPF_LSM
#   (init/Kconfig:1954). Present at gts4lv_defconfig:793,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:5726.
CONFIG_SECURITY=y

# --- 3.5 for KPROBES and BPF_JIT ---------------------------------------------
# MODULES - init/Kconfig:2285 @ baa585f67e0e, "menuconfig MODULES" (so grep for
#   "^menuconfig MODULES$"). dep of KPROBES (arch/Kconfig:44) and of BPF_JIT
#   (net/Kconfig:300). Present at gts4lv_defconfig:49,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:299.
CONFIG_MODULES=y

# --- 3.6 for DEBUG_INFO_BTF --------------------------------------------------
# DEBUG_INFO - lib/Kconfig.debug:127 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of DEBUG_INFO_BTF
#   (lib/Kconfig.debug:179). Present at gts4lv_defconfig:775,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:5495.
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO=y

# --- 3.7 for FUSE_BPF -------------------------------------------------------
# FUSE_FS - fs/fuse/Kconfig:1 @ baa585f67e0e. tristate. dep of FUSE_BPF
#   (fs/fuse/Kconfig:22). Present at gts4lv_defconfig:758,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:5316.
CONFIG_FUSE_FS=y

# --- 3.8 for NET_ACT_BPF -----------------------------------------------------
# NET_CLS_ACT - net/sched/Kconfig:605 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of NET_ACT_BPF
#   (net/sched/Kconfig:730). Present at gts4lv_defconfig:241,
#   gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:1128.
CONFIG_NET_CLS_ACT=y

# --- 3.9 for UCLAMP_TASK -----------------------------------------------------
# CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL - drivers/cpufreq/Kconfig:255 @ baa585f67e0e. dep of
#   UCLAMP_TASK (init/Kconfig:974); itself needs CPU_FREQ && SMP (:257), and
#   CPU_FREQ=y is at gts4lv_defconfig:95 / gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:674.
#   Present at gts4lv_defconfig:97, gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:693.
CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y

# --- 3.10 for USERFAULTFD (and ANDROID_BINDER_IPC) ---------------------------
# MMU - arch/arm64/Kconfig:128 @ baa585f67e0e, "def_bool y" (it is a per-arch
#   symbol, not in init/Kconfig). dep of USERFAULTFD (init/Kconfig:2011) and of
#   ANDROID_BINDER_IPC (drivers/android/Kconfig:12).
#   Pinned explicitly anyway; both eur_open files also state it
#   (gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:8).
CONFIG_MMU=y


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 4 - the 3 requested "turn off" options
#
# Appended AFTER the existing lines, which is what makes them win:
#   gts4lv_defconfig:28  CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED=y
#   gts4lv_defconfig:34  CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE=y
#   gts4lv_defconfig:24  CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHEDTUNE=y
# kconfig reads a defconfig in ONE top-to-bottom pass in which the last line for a
# symbol wins. scripts/kconfig/confdata.c @ baa585f67e0e: conf_read_simple()
# (:251) resets every symbol to tri=no (:310), then sets tri=no for each
# "# CONFIG_X is not set" line (:343, tested at :324) and calls conf_set_sym_val()
# (:374) for each "CONFIG_X=y" line, which sets tri=yes (confdata.c:126-148).
# =============================================================================

# --- 4.1 USER_NS ------------------------------------------------------------
# init/Kconfig:1476 @ baa585f67e0e: "config USER_NS / bool ... / default n",
# no dependencies, so there is nothing to switch on first and nothing to break.
# It is already n everywhere: no line at all in gts4lv_defconfig /
# gts4lvwifi_defconfig (the Kconfig default does it), and
# "# CONFIG_USER_NS is not set" at gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:163.
# So this line documents intent and is otherwise a no-op. Android does not want
# user namespaces.
# CONFIG_USER_NS is not set

# --- 4.2 RT_GROUP_SCHED - deliberate resolution of the contradiction ---------
# init/Kconfig:1294-1297 @ baa585f67e0e: "config RT_GROUP_SCHED / bool /
# depends on CGROUP_SCHED / default n". It sits inside the "if CGROUP_SCHED"
# block (which closes at init/Kconfig:1305).
# THE CONTRADICTION: gts4lv_defconfig:28 and gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:154 both
# say CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED=y, while this task's option list says turn it off.
# That line is currently DEAD, because CGROUP_SCHED was n and
# RT_GROUP_SCHED depends on it. Section 2.8 sets CGROUP_SCHED=y (it is mandatory
# anyway - see BLOCKER 3), which would REVIVE the stale =y.
# WHAT I DID AND WHY: turn it off, with the line uncommented, so the later
#   "# ... is not set" overrides gts4lv_defconfig:28.
#   Reasons, all sourced:
#   1. The ExyHyperBrick reference defconfig that the option list was derived
#      from has no RT_GROUP_SCHED line at all
#      (arch/arm64/configs/exynos9810-starlte_defconfig @ baa585f67e0e), i.e. it
#      takes the Kconfig default of n, while the same file does explicitly pin
#      BLK_CGROUP (:27), CGROUP_SCHED (:28) and BPF_JIT (:236).
#   2. The trial README lists CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED as one of the three things
#      the series disables.
#   3. Switching it on is not free: kernel/sched/rt.c has 23
#      "#ifdef CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED" blocks at baa585f67e0e (15 in sdm670) and
#      kernel/sched/core.c has many more (e.g. core.c:698, :5020, :8571, :9286).
#      That is newly compiled C code in the exact subsystem the series rewrites
#      hardest - 14 of the 150 conflicts are in kernel/sched.
#   4. RT group scheduling also blocks non-root RT scheduling until bandwidth is
#      allocated (its own help text, init/Kconfig:1299-1300), which is a
#      behaviour change Android does not ask for.
#   To go the other way: delete this line and keep gts4lv_defconfig:28. Expect
#   kernel/sched/rt.c and core.c to need build fixes.
# CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED is not set

# --- 4.3 SCHED_TUNE ---------------------------------------------------------
# init/Kconfig:1520-1523 @ baa585f67e0e: "config SCHED_TUNE / bool /
# depends on !UCLAMP_TASK / depends on SMP", no default, so it is n by default.
# Section 1.9 sets UCLAMP_TASK=y, which makes SCHED_TUNE unreachable *by
# Kconfig* - this is the "SCHED_TUNE (replaced by uclamp)" note in the trial
# README. gts4lv_defconfig:34 (CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE=y) and
# gts4lvwifi_defconfig:34 therefore become dead lines.
# Written out anyway, so the defconfig stops asserting something that is not
# true. No build impact either way.
# CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE is not set

# --- 4.4 CGROUP_SCHEDTUNE - dies with SCHED_TUNE, written for clarity --------
# init/Kconfig:1182-1184 @ baa585f67e0e: "config CGROUP_SCHEDTUNE / bool /
# depends on SCHED_TUNE". No default, so it is n once SCHED_TUNE is gone.
# gts4lv_defconfig:24 and gts4lv_eur_open_defconfig:145 say =y and become dead.
# Also a kernel/sched code change: kernel/sched/Makefile @ baa585f67e0e has
# "obj-$(CONFIG_SCHED_TUNE) += tune.o", which stops being built.
# CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHEDTUNE is not set


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 5 - optional lines, left commented. Uncomment only if you hit the
#             problem described. Do not uncomment them "just in case".
# =============================================================================

# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES is not set
#   lib/Kconfig.debug:185-188 @ baa585f67e0e: "default y", "depends on
#   DEBUG_INFO_BTF && MODULES", so it switches ITSELF on as soon as
#   section 1.4 and 3.5 are applied. That runs pahole on every single .ko and
#   its help text wants pahole 1.19 or later (lib/Kconfig.debug:193) - a
#   HIGHER bar than the v1.13 that vmlinux itself needs. If module BTF
#   generation fails on the build host, uncomment this line.

# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF is not set
#   The escape hatch if pahole cannot be installed on the build host at all.
#   Do NOT use it as the first answer: without vmlinux BTF, bpfloader on
#   Android 16 has nothing to work with. Fix the host tool first
#   (scripts/link-vmlinux.sh:209,214 @ baa585f67e0e).

# Do NOT touch PERF_EVENTS or KPROBE_EVENTS (sections 2.1/2.2) to work around a
#   TRACING pull-in problem: BPF_LSM cannot be built without them. The ftrace
#   code they bring in is a kernel-size cost, not a correctness problem.
